<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mulde</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mulde is a river in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, formed by the junction of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwickauer-mulde">Zwickauer Mulde</a> and the Freiberger Mulde in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>. It flows north through Saxony and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>, past Grimma and Eilenburg, and joins the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dessau">Dessau</a>. In August 2002 it caused severe flooding along its course.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mulde.jpg" alt="Mulde" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alma · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mulde_dueben1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
